00:35:50.820 --> 00:35:52.920
and drugging Stanley to get him to this meeting.
把斯坦利麻醉，好带他去开会。

812
00:35:53.180 --> 00:35:53.540
Yeah.
没错。

813
00:35:53.680 --> 00:35:55.100
Dwight walks into the break room.
德怀特走进休息室。

814
00:35:55.240 --> 00:35:56.280
Clark is standing there.
克拉克正站在那儿。

815
00:35:56.440 --> 00:36:00.060
Clark has one of my favorite lines in the episode, in this scene.
在这一幕里，克拉克有一句我最喜欢的台词。

816
00:36:00.240 --> 00:36:00.580
What?
什么？

817
00:36:00.580 --> 00:36:05.360
When Dwight says, Stanley, one way or another, you're going to come with me to make this sale.
当德怀特说，斯坦利，不管用什么方法，你都得跟我去完成这笔销售。

818
00:36:05.600 --> 00:36:10.280
Stanley goes past and then Clark says, hey, can you just let me out of here before whatever
斯坦利走过去，然后克拉克说，嘿，能不能在接下来的事情

819
00:36:10.280 --> 00:36:11.040
comes next?
发生之前先让我离开这儿？

820
00:36:11.500 --> 00:36:11.780
Yeah.
没错。

821
00:36:12.240 --> 00:36:18.900
Because Dwight's got this ridiculously long tranquilizer gun and he shoots Stanley three
因为德怀特拿着一把长得离谱的麻醉枪，他朝斯坦利开了

822
00:36:18.900 --> 00:36:19.520
times.
三枪。

823
00:36:19.520 --> 00:36:21.240
With little red dart things.
用的是那种红色的小飞镖。

824
00:36:21.520 --> 00:36:22.780
And then Stanley collapses.
然后斯坦利就倒下了。

825
00:36:23.600 --> 00:36:26.800
And Dwight says to Clark, don't worry, Andy approved this.
德怀特对克拉克说，别担心，安迪批准了。

826
00:36:27.400 --> 00:36:30.140
Well, we got a lot of mail about this, as you can imagine.
嗯，正如你所料，我们收到了很多关于这部分的来信。

827
00:36:30.140 --> 00:36:30.980
David H.
来自英国的戴维·H.

828
00:36:31.120 --> 00:36:35.340
from England said, how did you create the illusion of Stanley being shot with darts?
问，你们是怎么制造出斯坦利被飞镖射中这种错觉的？

829
00:36:35.660 --> 00:36:37.100
And Lily B.G.
还有来自加拿大的莉莉·B.G.

830
00:36:37.300 --> 00:36:41.840
from Canada said, what was used for the bull tranquilizers when Dwight shoots
问，德怀特射击斯坦利时，

831
00:36:41.840 --> 00:36:42.280
Stanley?
那些公牛镇静剂是用什么做的？

832
00:36:42.560 --> 00:36:45.660
Well, Steve Burgess said it was visual effects.
嗯，史蒂夫·伯吉斯说那是视觉特效。

833
00:36:46.260 --> 00:36:49.860
We did not actually shoot anything at Leslie David Baker.
我们并没有真的向莱斯利·大卫·贝克射击任何东西。

834
00:36:50.900 --> 00:36:52.360
We filmed the dart.
我们拍摄了飞镖。

835
00:36:52.580 --> 00:36:53.680
We filmed Stanley.
我们拍摄了斯坦利。

836
00:36:54.000 --> 00:36:56.240
We attached the dart to his clothes.
我们把飞镖粘在他的衣服上。

837
00:36:56.400 --> 00:37:02.480
And then in post-production, it looks like the darts going into him.
然后在后期制作中，看起来就像飞镖射进了他身体里一样。

838
00:37:02.660 --> 00:37:03.040
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

839
00:37:03.060 --> 00:37:04.320
It was all visual effects.
全都是视觉特效。

840
00:37:04.900 --> 00:37:09.460
As far as the moment when Leslie is tranquilized, Matt Soane said the first thing they had to
至于莱斯利被麻醉的那一刻，马特·索恩说他们首先要

841
00:37:09.460 --> 00:37:11.320
figure out was this dart gun.
解决的就是这把飞镖枪。

842
00:37:11.520 --> 00:37:12.400
Here's what he said.
他是这么说的。

843
00:37:12.400 --> 00:37:22.120
We had a lot of conversations about the dart gun to make it feel as much of a benign weapon
我们讨论了很多关于飞镖枪的问题，为了让它看起来尽可能像是一种无害的武器。

844
00:37:22.120 --> 00:37:22.880
as possible.
我们不想让德怀特拿着一把真正的枪或步枪。

845
00:37:23.040 --> 00:37:27.240
We didn't want a real gun or a rifle for Dwight to have.
所以我们构思出了这个版本的飞镖枪。

846
00:37:27.460 --> 00:37:34.340
So we sort of concocted this version of what this dart gun was.
这就是我们最终想出来的方案。

847
00:37:34.460 --> 00:37:36.260
And that was what we came up with.
没错，史蒂夫说我们尝试了几种不同的飞镖枪选项。

848
00:37:37.240 --> 00:37:41.400
Yeah, Steve said we went through a few different dart gun options.
电视台给出的意见是，他们不希望这看起来像真正的武器。

849
00:37:42.160 --> 00:37:47.260
The network had given a note that they didn't want this to look like an actual weapon.
所以菲尔·谢伊找到了我们最终使用的这一款。

850
00:37:47.680 --> 00:37:50.460
And so Phil Shea found this one that we used.
所以菲尔·谢伊找到了我们最终使用的这一款。

851
00:37:50.540 --> 00:37:52.480
It looked kind of like a dart shooter.
看起来有点像个飞镖发射器。

852
00:37:52.680 --> 00:37:55.420
It had that really long, kind of like skinny barrel.
它有一个非常长、有点细的枪管。

853
00:37:55.420 --> 00:37:56.780
It was very cartoonish.
看起来非常卡通。

854
00:37:57.060 --> 00:37:57.820
Yeah, exactly.
没错，确实如此。

855
00:37:58.700 --> 00:38:02.300
Matt Soane also talked about how Leslie really sold this moment.
马特·索恩也谈到了莱斯利是如何出色地演绎了这一刻的。

856
00:38:02.300 --> 00:38:03.620
I thought he did fantastic.
我觉得他演得太棒了。

857
00:38:03.640 --> 00:38:04.960
Let's hear what Matt said.
让我们听听马特是怎么说的。

858
00:38:05.740 --> 00:38:12.380
Leslie did an amazing collapse and fall into a pad that we had set up.
莱斯利完成了一次精彩的倒地，摔在了我们准备好的垫子上。

859
00:38:12.540 --> 00:38:17.120
And we did it a couple times, but he really enjoyed the moment and had fun with it.
我们拍了好几次，但他真的很享受那一刻，玩得很开心。

860
00:38:17.240 --> 00:38:21.480
I feel like for this episode, this was something that was very different for Leslie.
我觉得对于这一集来说，这对莱斯利来说是非常不同的一次经历。

861
00:38:21.760 --> 00:38:30.700
And again, it gave us a fun moment to see Rain and Clark Duke have another buddy moment like
再说一次，这让我们看到了雷恩和克拉克·杜克又一次像在“西装仓库”那一集里一样，

862
00:38:30.700 --> 00:38:32.580
they did in Suit Warehouse.
有了那种哥们儿间的互动时刻。

863
00:38:32.580 --> 00:38:38.480
I think that Clark's reaction in the break room as all this is going down was great.
我觉得当这一切发生时，克拉克在休息室里的反应非常棒。

864
00:38:38.920 --> 00:38:42.700
Well, I agree that Leslie was excellent in the scene.
嗯，我同意莱斯利在这一幕中表现得非常出色。

865
00:38:42.840 --> 00:38:44.200
I mean, when he falls forward.
我是说，当他向前倒下的时候。

866
00:38:44.600 --> 00:38:44.840
Yeah.
是的。

867
00:38:45.100 --> 00:38:48.540
You don't see him like brace himself with his hands or anything.
你没看到他用手撑住自己之类的动作。

868
00:38:48.800 --> 00:38:49.960
I mean, that is hard to do.
我是说，这很难做到。

869
00:38:49.960 --> 00:38:58.600
This is now going to set off a dilemma for Dwight, which is how does he get Stanley from the break room
这现在给德怀特带来了一个难题，那就是他该如何把躺在地板上的斯坦利，

870
00:38:58.600 --> 00:39:02.860
on the floor all the way down to the car and into a meeting?
从休息室一路弄到车里去参加会议呢？

871
00:39:03.360 --> 00:39:05.920
So maybe we should describe how he does that.
所以也许我们应该描述一下他是怎么做的。

872
00:39:06.360 --> 00:39:06.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

873
00:39:06.980 --> 00:39:10.780
He starts by somehow getting Clark to help him.
他首先想办法让克拉克帮他。

874
00:39:11.600 --> 00:39:11.820
Yeah.
是的。

875
00:39:12.020 --> 00:39:12.960
Clark witnessed this.
克拉克目睹了这一切。

876
00:39:12.960 --> 00:39:13.880
He's in it now.
他现在也卷进来了。

877
00:39:14.220 --> 00:39:14.520
Yeah.
没错。

878
00:39:14.840 --> 00:39:17.900
They're trying to move him by hand and it is not working.
他们试图用手搬动他，但根本行不通。

879
00:39:17.940 --> 00:39:18.300
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

880
00:39:19.160 --> 00:39:21.100
So they get a rolly office chair.
于是他们找来了一把带轮子的办公椅。

881
00:39:21.480 --> 00:39:25.860
I also want to give props to Leslie David Baker for his acting in the rolly chair.
我也想给莱斯利·大卫·贝克在办公椅上的表演点个赞。

882
00:39:26.260 --> 00:39:26.820
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

883
00:39:27.340 --> 00:39:28.080
All of it.
全程都是。

884
00:39:28.200 --> 00:39:32.700
He had to just be out of it while they're tugging him and having dialogue around him.
当他们拉扯他并在他身边对话时，他必须保持那种昏迷的状态。

885
00:39:32.700 --> 00:39:33.900
I thought he did fantastic.
我觉得他演得太棒了。

886
00:39:34.260 --> 00:39:35.520
The rolly chair works.
办公椅派上了用场。

887
00:39:35.520 --> 00:39:37.300
But remember, the elevator's broken.
但别忘了，电梯坏了。

888
00:39:37.300 --> 00:39:39.040
How are they going to get him down the stairs?
他们要怎么把他弄下楼梯呢？

889
00:39:39.040 --> 00:39:39.700
Yeah.
是啊。

890
00:39:40.140 --> 00:39:47.080
What happens is I guess Dwight makes a cardboard ramp and now they need to wrap Stanley in bubble wrap
发生的事情是，我猜德怀特做了一个纸板坡道，现在他们需要用气泡膜把斯坦利包起来，

891
00:39:47.080 --> 00:39:49.380
and they're going to strap a helmet onto his head.
还要给他戴上头盔。

892
00:39:49.700 --> 00:39:52.620
This looks like something out of that movie Jackass.
这看起来就像电影《蠢蛋搞怪秀》里的场景。

893
00:39:52.860 --> 00:39:54.040
It really does.
确实很像。

894
00:39:54.440 --> 00:39:59.480
And while they're discussing the best way to kind of slide him down the stairs,
就在他们讨论把他滑下楼梯的最佳方式时，

895
00:39:59.480 --> 00:40:02.340
Stanley slides down the stairs on his own.
斯坦利自己滑下楼梯去了。

896
00:40:02.400 --> 00:40:03.160
By accident.
是意外。

897
00:40:03.480 --> 00:40:05.340
And his head goes into the wall.
而且他的头撞进了墙里。

898
00:40:05.780 --> 00:40:06.900
And leaves a divot.
还在墙上留下了一个坑。

899
00:40:06.900 --> 00:40:09.880
But eventually they get him down to the parking lot and into the car.
但最终他们还是把他弄到了停车场并送进了车里。

900
00:40:10.160 --> 00:40:11.540
We had a fan mail flurry.
我们收到了一大波粉丝来信。

901
00:40:11.740 --> 00:40:12.340
I bet.
我敢打赌。

902
00:40:12.860 --> 00:40:16.920
Basically, people said, please give us all the details on the Stanley stunts.
基本上，大家都在说，请给我们详细讲讲斯坦利的特技镜头。

903
00:40:17.160 --> 00:40:21.840
What stunts did Leslie David Baker do versus the ones a stunt double did?
莱斯利·大卫·贝克本人做了哪些特技，哪些又是替身做的？

904
00:40:22.640 --> 00:40:25.840
Well, lucky for us, Matt Stone broke it all down.
嗯，幸运的是，马特·斯通把这些都拆解说明了。

905
00:40:25.840 --> 00:40:27.200
And here's what he had to say.
以下是他的说法。

906
00:40:27.200 --> 00:40:34.700
We have moments where we used the real Stanley, but we also had a stuntman playing Stanley.
有些镜头我们用了真正的斯坦利，但也有镜头是替身演员扮演的。

907
00:40:34.920 --> 00:40:40.800
And it was the stuntman whose head we sort of ran into the wall in the break room.
在休息室里撞墙的镜头，其实是替身演员。

908
00:40:41.000 --> 00:40:50.460
But Leslie did all of his own stuff when they were dropping him into the chair and pushing him down the hall.
但当他们把莱斯利扔进椅子并推着他在走廊里走时，都是他本人完成的。

909
00:40:50.460 --> 00:40:59.900
When it came to the stairwell slide, we had discussed many different options on how to do this.
说到楼梯间的滑行，我们讨论过很多种实现方案。

910
00:41:00.280 --> 00:41:05.740
We had the stuntman, so we talked about using the stuntman to slide down.
我们有替身演员，所以讨论过让他来滑。

911
00:41:05.900 --> 00:41:11.800
But the problem was that it was too dangerous of a slide because whoever was going to do it,
但问题是这个滑行太危险了，因为无论谁来做，

912
00:41:11.900 --> 00:41:15.040
their arms were trapped in the bubble wrap by their side.
他们的手臂都会被气泡膜束缚在身体两侧。

913
00:41:15.040 --> 00:41:23.680
So we ultimately figured it was the safest to build a dummy to slide down the ramp and hit the wall,
所以我们最终认为，最安全的办法是做一个假人，让它滑下坡道并撞上墙壁，

914
00:41:23.720 --> 00:41:29.060
which is ultimately what we did and managed to hide Stanley's face.
这正是我们最终采取的做法，而且成功遮住了斯坦利的脸。

915
00:41:29.280 --> 00:41:41.580
And then we have the cutaway after the fact of Leslie wrapped up in the helmet by the hole that we punched in the wall.
之后我们切到了莱斯利被包裹着、戴着头盔，出现在墙上那个洞旁边的镜头。

916
00:41:41.580 --> 00:41:48.260
Now, getting Stanley into the car, Leslie played great at being passed out.
至于把斯坦利塞进车里，莱斯利演得非常棒，就像真的昏过去了一样。

917
00:41:48.600 --> 00:41:55.920
And, you know, it was a challenge for both Clark and Rain because Leslie didn't have a lot of control
而且，这对克拉克和雷恩来说也是个挑战，因为莱斯利无法控制身体，

918
00:41:55.920 --> 00:41:58.880
because he was in the bubble wrap and his arms were by his side.
因为他被气泡膜裹着，手臂动弹不得。

919
00:41:58.920 --> 00:42:04.680
And they had to sort of maneuver him around and attempt to get him into the car.
他们不得不费力地挪动他，试图把他塞进车里。

920
00:42:04.900 --> 00:42:08.860
We did that in a lot of edits as well, which kind of sold the moment.
我们通过大量的剪辑完成了这一段，这让那一刻看起来很真实。

921
00:42:10.140 --> 00:42:11.900
I have to say, I thought it was seamless.
我不得不说，我觉得这天衣无缝。

922
00:42:12.720 --> 00:42:12.980
Yeah.
是啊。

923
00:42:13.420 --> 00:42:16.480
I mean, it was a dummy.
我是说，那是个假人。

924
00:42:16.780 --> 00:42:17.160
Right.
没错。

925
00:42:17.300 --> 00:42:18.960
A stunt double and Leslie.
替身演员和莱斯利。

926
00:42:19.260 --> 00:42:20.300
They did a great job.
他们做得太棒了。

927
00:42:20.600 --> 00:42:21.380
And I could never tell.
我完全看不出来。

928
00:42:21.640 --> 00:42:21.780
Yeah.
是啊。

929
00:42:22.260 --> 00:42:25.120
Steve said Leslie's stunt double was Buddy Sawstand.
史蒂夫说莱斯利的替身演员是巴迪·索斯坦德。

930
00:42:25.340 --> 00:42:27.660
Brett Jones was our stunt coordinator for this episode.
布雷特·琼斯是我们这一集的特技协调员。

931
00:42:27.980 --> 00:42:31.820
I got a little curious about the Stanley dummy that Matt talked about.
我对马特提到的那个斯坦利假人有点好奇。

932
00:42:32.060 --> 00:42:34.000
So I reached out to Steve Burgess.
所以我联系了史蒂夫·伯吉斯。

933
00:42:34.000 --> 00:42:40.160
Because I was like, did Leslie have to do that thing where you get like a face cast made?
因为我在想，莱斯利是不是得去做那种脸部翻模？

934
00:42:40.300 --> 00:42:43.000
Or, you know, you've seen that before, right?
或者，你知道的，你以前见过那种吧？

935
00:42:43.560 --> 00:42:46.840
Steve Burgess said Phil actually used a dummy that he already had.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说，菲尔其实用的是他现有的一个假人。

936
00:42:47.000 --> 00:42:52.740
And since it was wrapped up in bubble wrap and wearing a helmet, it kind of worked.
既然它被气泡膜裹着又戴着头盔，效果还挺好的。

937
00:42:52.900 --> 00:42:53.780
It sold it.
足以以假乱真了。

938
00:42:53.900 --> 00:42:57.860
So no, Leslie did not have to sit through some 12-hour molding of his face.
所以不用，莱斯利没必要去忍受长达12小时的脸部翻模过程。

939
00:42:58.880 --> 00:43:02.840
Obviously, all the shots where we see a face are Leslie.
显然，所有能看到脸的镜头都是莱斯利本人。

940
00:43:03.220 --> 00:43:05.700
The slide down the stairs is the dummy.
滑下楼梯的是假人。

941
00:43:06.160 --> 00:43:10.640
But then when we cut back to the dummy at the end of the stairs, that was Leslie again.
但当我们在楼梯尽头切回假人镜头时，那又是莱斯利本人了。

942
00:43:10.920 --> 00:43:12.200
It was just amazing.
这简直太神奇了。

943
00:43:13.440 --> 00:43:18.040
We did get another fan question about this sequence, Angela, from Jenna F.
安吉拉，我们还收到了另一位粉丝关于这段戏的提问，来自洛杉矶的珍娜·F。

944
00:43:18.140 --> 00:43:18.880
in Los Angeles.
在洛杉矶。

945
00:43:19.460 --> 00:43:20.820
She writes in a lot.
她经常写信来。

946
00:43:20.820 --> 00:43:33.700
Yeah, she noticed that Rain slid down the cardboard and really felt like this was something Rain might have done on the fly that made everyone freak out.
是啊，她注意到雷恩滑下纸板的动作，感觉这像是雷恩临时起意做的，把大家都吓坏了。

947
00:43:34.280 --> 00:43:36.760
I asked Matt Soane about it, and here's what he said.
我问了马特·索恩这件事，他是这么说的。

948
00:43:36.880 --> 00:43:37.880
Are you the Jenna F.
你就是那个在洛杉矶的珍娜·F吗？

949
00:43:37.980 --> 00:43:38.680
in Los Angeles?
这真是个巧合。

950
00:43:39.300 --> 00:43:40.420
It's a coincidence.
这真是个巧合。

951
00:43:42.460 --> 00:43:45.760
Rain really wanted to slide down the stairs.
Rain真的很想从楼梯上滑下去。

952
00:43:46.520 --> 00:43:54.800
And I feel like production told him not to, but he did it anyway, and it was sort of within the scene.
我觉得制作组告诉过他不要那样做，但他还是做了，而且这看起来像是戏里的一部分。

953
00:43:55.060 --> 00:43:56.020
It was very funny.
这非常有趣。

954
00:43:56.240 --> 00:44:02.920
But again, production wants to keep the actors safe, and it was a long slide.
但话说回来，制作组想要保证演员的安全，而且那段滑梯很长。

955
00:44:03.540 --> 00:44:04.620
Rain did the slide.
Rain还是滑了。

956
00:44:04.620 --> 00:44:05.940
I think he enjoyed it.
我想他很享受这个过程。

957
00:44:06.000 --> 00:44:11.260
I think he did it maybe twice, but I'm not sure it could have also been our last take.
我觉得他可能滑了两次，但我不确定，那也可能是我们的最后一条拍摄。

958
00:44:11.260 --> 00:44:15.540
Because I feel like we had discussed him sliding down, and he was told not to.
因为我觉得我们讨论过他滑下去的事，而且他被告知不能那样做。

959
00:44:16.300 --> 00:44:22.140
But he did it anyway, and it made the cut, and it was very funny and felt realistic.
但他还是做了，而且这一幕被剪进了正片，非常搞笑，感觉也很真实。

960
00:44:24.640 --> 00:44:24.800
Yeah.
没错。

961
00:44:25.260 --> 00:44:28.060
Steve Burgess also confirmed that Rain did it on the fly.
Steve Burgess也证实了Rain是临时起意做的。

962
00:44:28.400 --> 00:44:36.640
Well, I was filming over on that side, you know, with the senator in the parking lot, and I distinctly remember our crew guys sliding down it.
嗯，当时我在那边拍摄，你知道的，和参议员在停车场，我清楚地记得我们的工作人员滑了下去。

963
00:44:36.860 --> 00:44:42.860
Steve Burgess said that that was why they weren't that concerned when Rain did it, because the crew had been doing it all day.
Steve Burgess说这就是为什么当Rain滑下去时他们并不那么担心，因为工作人员整天都在滑。

964
00:44:43.020 --> 00:44:43.220
Yep.
没错。

965
00:44:44.060 --> 00:44:50.740
Well, why don't we take a break, and when we come back, we're going to get some real therapy session for Jim and Pam.
好了，我们休息一下，回来后，我们要为Jim和Pam进行一次真正的心理治疗。

966
00:44:51.000 --> 00:44:53.220
Yeah, couples therapy when we're back.
没错，回来后进行夫妻心理治疗。

967
00:44:53.460 --> 00:44:53.620
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

968
00:45:04.500 --> 00:45:08.220
I'd like to start by saying I finally feel normal again.
我想先说一下，我终于感觉恢复正常了。

969
00:45:08.700 --> 00:45:09.020
Oh.
哦。

970
00:45:09.560 --> 00:45:11.680
From the nasty drink that we drank.
就是因为我们喝的那种难喝的饮料。

971
00:45:11.860 --> 00:45:12.180
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

972
00:45:12.360 --> 00:45:12.640
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

973
00:45:12.960 --> 00:45:16.160
And I know we said it last week, I love our space.
我知道我们上周说过，我爱我们的空间。

974
00:45:17.060 --> 00:45:25.260
When I was coming in today from the car, I had an encounter, and it was so charming, and it just made me love our new studio even more.
今天我从车里走过来的时候，遇到了一件事，非常迷人，这让我更加爱我们的新工作室了。

975
00:45:25.260 --> 00:45:26.240
What was it?
是什么事？

976
00:45:26.740 --> 00:45:31.220
Okay, so, you know, we're located in a little bit of a touristy area.
好吧，你知道，我们位于一个稍微有点游客气息的地区。

977
00:45:31.400 --> 00:45:32.020
We are.
确实是。

978
00:45:32.620 --> 00:45:38.940
And there was a family on the street, and they were looking at their phone, and they looked like tourists to me.
街上有一家人，他们正在看手机，在我看来他们像是游客。

979
00:45:39.160 --> 00:45:39.420
Right.
对。

980
00:45:39.800 --> 00:45:43.320
And I thought, oh, I'm going to say hi to them.
我想，哦，我要去跟他们打个招呼。

981
00:45:43.460 --> 00:45:45.100
I'm going to ask them if they need directions.
我要问问他们是否需要指路。

982
00:45:45.480 --> 00:45:46.840
Because they looked a little loSt.
因为他们看起来有点迷路了。

983
00:45:46.940 --> 00:45:47.460
A little bit.
有一点。

984
00:45:47.560 --> 00:45:47.860
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

985
00:45:47.860 --> 00:45:51.920
So I said, hey, are you traveling?
所以我说，嘿，你们在旅行吗？

986
00:45:52.260 --> 00:45:53.080
Are you tourists?
你们是游客吗？

987
00:45:53.520 --> 00:45:54.800
And they looked at me for a second.
他们看了我一眼。

988
00:45:54.880 --> 00:45:55.640
They kind of paused.
他们停顿了一下。

989
00:45:55.680 --> 00:45:59.400
And then they explained that they were French, that they didn't really speak English.
然后他们解释说他们是法国人，不太会说英语。

990
00:45:59.600 --> 00:46:01.320
And I said, oh.
我说，哦。

991
00:46:01.860 --> 00:46:02.200
Bonjour.
Bonjour（你好）。

992
00:46:02.560 --> 00:46:03.400
I said, bonjour.
我说，Bonjour。

993
00:46:03.640 --> 00:46:07.420
Did all of a sudden your French come back to you like it did in that market in France?
你那法语突然又回来了，就像在法国那个市场里一样吗？

994
00:46:07.560 --> 00:46:08.260
I was hoping.
我当时正希望如此。

995
00:46:08.600 --> 00:46:10.540
And I said, je parle un peu de français.
我说，je parle un peu de français（我会说一点法语）。

996
00:46:10.940 --> 00:46:13.240
And she said, I speak a little English.
她说，我会说一点英语。

997
00:46:13.460 --> 00:46:16.120
And then I said, très un peu de français.
然后我说，très un peu de français（非常一点法语）。

998
00:46:16.180 --> 00:46:17.360
Very little French.
法语说得很少。

999
00:46:17.360 --> 00:46:20.240
And the man said, un petit de français.
那个人说，un petit de français（一点点法语）。

1000
00:46:20.900 --> 00:46:25.040
And I said, oui, petit de français, not très un peu.
我说，oui（是的），petit de français，不是très un peu。

1001
00:46:25.740 --> 00:46:27.800
But anyway, we had a moment.
总之，我们当时聊得挺投缘。

1002
00:46:27.940 --> 00:46:29.300
They were looking for the Walk of Fame.
他们在找星光大道。

1003
00:46:29.480 --> 00:46:33.080
I was able to give them directions using au gauche and au droit.
我用法语的“向左”和“向右”给他们指了路。

1004
00:46:33.400 --> 00:46:34.840
I was very proud of myself.
我当时特别有成就感。

1005
00:46:35.120 --> 00:46:37.940
And then I did a crazy thing, lady.
然后我做了一件疯狂的事，女士。

1006
00:46:38.080 --> 00:46:38.720
Is this crazy?
这算疯狂吗？

1007
00:46:39.200 --> 00:46:42.900
I said, do y'all watch The Office in France?
我问他们，你们在法国看《办公室》吗？

1008
00:46:43.160 --> 00:46:44.240
You did not.
你居然问了？

1009
00:46:44.360 --> 00:46:44.860
I did.
我问了。

1010
00:46:45.020 --> 00:46:46.240
This is not like you.
这可不像你。

1011
00:46:46.240 --> 00:46:48.660
You are Miss Fly under the radar.
你平时可是那种“低调行事”的小姐。

1012
00:46:49.040 --> 00:46:49.620
I know.
我知道。

1013
00:46:49.620 --> 00:46:54.460
But I'm like, if you're a tourist and you've come from France and you're walking to the
但我当时想，如果你是个游客，从法国大老远跑来，正走在去

1014
00:46:54.460 --> 00:47:00.140
Hollywood Walk of Fame and you've run into an actor or an actress, don't you want a picture
好莱坞星光大道的路上，结果碰巧遇到了一个演员，难道你不想和

1015
00:47:00.140 --> 00:47:00.920
with that person?
那个人合影吗？

1016
00:47:01.200 --> 00:47:01.940
Maybe so.
也许吧。

1017
00:47:02.060 --> 00:47:02.520
What happened?
后来怎么样了？

1018
00:47:02.520 --> 00:47:06.460
They don't watch The Office, seem to have never heard of it.
他们不看《办公室》，好像听都没听说过。

1019
00:47:06.460 --> 00:47:08.240
They think you work in an office.
他们以为你在办公室上班呢。

1020
00:47:08.500 --> 00:47:10.800
So, I kid you not.
所以，我没骗你。

1021
00:47:10.800 --> 00:47:16.500
I doubled down and I Googled myself and I showed my phone to them.
我豁出去了，直接谷歌了一下自己，然后把手机给他们看。

1022
00:47:16.740 --> 00:47:17.220
Jenna Fisher.
珍娜·费舍。

1023
00:47:17.220 --> 00:47:18.640
I said, this is me.
我说，这就是我。

1024
00:47:18.800 --> 00:47:20.320
Who are you right now?
你现在到底是谁啊？

1025
00:47:20.320 --> 00:47:22.180
And they said, Jenna Fisher.
他们说，珍娜·费舍。

1026
00:47:22.780 --> 00:47:25.040
And I said, yes, that's me.
我说，对，就是我。

1027
00:47:25.240 --> 00:47:25.900
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍。

1028
00:47:26.300 --> 00:47:30.120
And then they got all excited and the two girls, they were like kind of teen girls.
然后他们就兴奋起来了，那两个女孩，看起来像是十几岁的少女。

1029
00:47:30.320 --> 00:47:32.440
They wanted a picture and we took a picture.
她们想要合影，我们就拍了一张。

1030
00:47:32.680 --> 00:47:36.420
And I could tell as they were walking away that they were like making a note to themselves.
我能看出来，她们走开的时候，心里肯定在暗自琢磨。

1031
00:47:36.740 --> 00:47:37.920
We've met Jenna Fisher.
我们见到珍娜·费舍了。

1032
00:47:38.220 --> 00:47:39.340
We don't know who she is.
我们不知道她是谁。

1033
00:47:39.500 --> 00:47:42.560
She might be a famous receptioniSt.
她可能是个有名的前台接待员吧。

1034
00:47:42.560 --> 00:47:43.900
Well, we don't know.
嗯，我们确实不知道。

1035
00:47:45.060 --> 00:47:47.560
But that was my little encounter on the way in.
不过这就是我来路上的一点小插曲。

1036
00:47:47.720 --> 00:47:48.880
That's so charming.
那太可爱了。

1037
00:47:49.020 --> 00:47:49.620
I don't know.
我不知道。

1038
00:47:50.780 --> 00:47:52.600
I can't believe you did that.
真不敢相信你居然那么做了。

1039
00:47:52.720 --> 00:47:57.120
Well, one of my favorite things to do is when we're driving somewhere and one of those like
其实，我最喜欢做的一件事就是，当我们开车去某处，旁边经过那些

1040
00:47:57.120 --> 00:48:03.060
tour buses, those like open air vans of tourists drive by and you're kind of at a stoplight
观光巴士，就是那种露天的游客车，正好在红绿灯路口停在一起时，

1041
00:48:03.060 --> 00:48:08.640
together, I always like to roll down my window and be like, hey, everybody, welcome to L.A.
我总喜欢摇下车窗，喊一声：嘿，大家好，欢迎来到洛杉矶。

1042
00:48:08.640 --> 00:48:14.140
Well, what I like to do is when I'm on vacation and I see a couple and they're also on vacation
我喜欢做的是，当我度假时，看到一对情侣也在度假，

1043
00:48:14.140 --> 00:48:18.360
and they're trying to do that thing that couples do where you take a selfie in front of some
他们正试图做情侣们常做的事，就是在某个美景前自拍，

1044
00:48:18.360 --> 00:48:21.960
beautiful thing, but you don't have someone to take it for you and you don't want to ask
但身边没人帮他们拍，他们又不好意思开口

1045
00:48:21.960 --> 00:48:22.740
someone maybe.
去麻烦别人。

1046
00:48:23.480 --> 00:48:28.120
I go up to that couple or family and I say, do you guys want a group picture?
我会走过去对那对情侣或那个家庭说，你们需要拍张合影吗？

1047
00:48:28.240 --> 00:48:29.040
I'll take it for you.
我帮你们拍吧。

1048
00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:31.560
And that's my favorite thing to do.
这是我最喜欢做的事。

1049
00:48:31.700 --> 00:48:35.440
And sometimes people recognize me and sometimes they don't, but I don't ever say anything.
有时候人们会认出我，有时候认不出，但我从来不会多说什么。

1050
00:48:35.760 --> 00:48:38.620
You don't get out your phone and Google yourself and explain who you are.
你不会掏出手机谷歌自己，然后解释你是谁。

1051
00:48:38.640 --> 00:48:43.140
I don't, but it's always fun when that moment happens.
我倒没有，但那种时刻出现时总是很有趣。

1052
00:48:43.720 --> 00:48:45.620
I just remember coming to L.A.
我只记得第一次和家人一起来洛杉矶的时候，

1053
00:48:45.760 --> 00:48:50.000
for the first time with my family and my sister and I think
当时我和我妹妹，我想，

1054
00:48:50.000 --> 00:48:56.620
I just saw myself in this family, you know, and how much I just wanted to run into some
我仿佛在那个家庭里看到了自己，你知道，我当时有多想偶遇某个

1055
00:48:56.620 --> 00:48:58.500
person from film and television.
影视圈的人。

1056
00:48:58.780 --> 00:49:02.040
If Julia Roberts had been like, do you need help with directions?
如果当时朱莉娅·罗伯茨问我：需要指路吗？

1057
00:49:02.380 --> 00:49:03.460
Well, you know who we ran into?
那你猜我们遇到了谁？

1058
00:49:04.080 --> 00:49:05.080
Diane Keaton.
黛安·基顿。

1059
00:49:05.340 --> 00:49:06.260
You and your family.
你和你家人。

1060
00:49:06.260 --> 00:49:11.020
We passed her on the street and my mom is convinced to this day that Diane Keaton admired
我们在街上和她擦肩而过，我妈至今都坚信黛安·基顿当时是在欣赏

1061
00:49:11.020 --> 00:49:11.560
her hat.
她的帽子。

1062
00:49:13.260 --> 00:49:14.280
Family story.
家族轶事。

1063
00:49:14.480 --> 00:49:15.340
It's legend.
这可是传奇。

1064
00:49:15.620 --> 00:49:15.740
Yeah.
是啊。

1065
00:49:15.860 --> 00:49:19.040
Remember that time Diane Keaton did a double take?
还记得黛安·基顿回头看那次吗？

1066
00:49:19.320 --> 00:49:20.580
Because she loved my hat.
因为她喜欢我的帽子。

1067
00:49:20.580 --> 00:49:21.220
She saw my hat.
她看到了我的帽子。

1068
00:49:23.000 --> 00:49:24.780
Well, where should we go?
那么，我们该聊点什么呢？

1069
00:49:25.160 --> 00:49:31.340
This very intense conversation is happening between Pam and Nellie and Jim and Toby.
帕姆、奈莉、吉姆和托比之间正在进行一场非常激烈的对话。

1070
00:49:31.940 --> 00:49:33.080
We're cutting back and forth.
我们正在来回切换镜头。

1071
00:49:33.380 --> 00:49:35.840
They're really sharing a lot of stuff, too.
他们分享的内容也确实很多。

1072
00:49:36.040 --> 00:49:39.540
Like, I'm just like, wow, this therapy session is going to be a big one.
我当时就想，哇，这次心理咨询肯定会是个大场面。

1073
00:49:40.080 --> 00:49:40.300
Yeah.
没错。

1074
00:49:40.480 --> 00:49:46.340
I mean, Pam kind of says, okay, Jim did this without asking me, this without asking me.
我是说，帕姆大概是说，好吧，吉姆没问我就做了这个，没问我就做了那个。

1075
00:49:46.400 --> 00:49:50.520
At what point does he stop getting rewarded for making big life decisions without me?
他到底要到什么时候才能停止这种不跟我商量就做人生重大决定的行为，还能得到奖励？

