1223
00:56:58.300 --> 00:57:00.580
And we've heard about him for a while now.
我们听说过他有一阵子了。

1224
00:57:01.360 --> 00:57:02.940
But boy, this was a shocker.
但天哪，这真是太令人震惊了。

1225
00:57:03.220 --> 00:57:03.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1226
00:57:03.420 --> 00:57:10.380
All of this betrayal of both Angela and Oscar is going to lead to some pretty fun stuff coming up in these next few episodes.
这种对安吉拉和奥斯卡的双重背叛，将会在接下来的几集里引出一些非常有趣的剧情。

1227
00:57:10.860 --> 00:57:14.220
Yes, because they used to have a common love, but now they're going to have a common enemy.
没错，因为他们曾经拥有共同的爱，但现在他们将拥有共同的敌人。

1228
00:57:14.580 --> 00:57:14.920
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1229
00:57:14.920 --> 00:57:17.300
Up next is such a hilarious scene.
接下来是一场非常搞笑的戏。

1230
00:57:17.760 --> 00:57:21.000
Andy has found what he hopes to be his new agent.
安迪找到了他心目中的新经纪人。

1231
00:57:21.380 --> 00:57:22.660
It's Carla Fern.
就是卡拉·弗恩。

1232
00:57:23.240 --> 00:57:26.160
This is how this scene is described in the shooting draft.
剧本初稿中是这样描述这场戏的。

1233
00:57:26.160 --> 00:57:35.900
It says Andy sits in a very narrow, bare-bones waiting room, some chairs, a dingy-looking water cooler, and a very plastic plant.
上面写着安迪坐在一个非常狭窄、简陋的候诊室里，里面有几把椅子、一个看起来很脏的饮水机，还有一盆塑料假花。

1234
00:57:36.260 --> 00:57:42.400
A mom reads a magazine as her freckled-faced redhead son, dressed in a jacket and tie, plays with her phone.
一位母亲正在看杂志，她那满脸雀斑、红头发的儿子穿着西装打着领带，正在玩她的手机。

1235
00:57:42.700 --> 00:57:50.460
Andy looks across the waiting room where a clean-cut man sits next to a live dog with a live cat on top,
安迪看向候诊室对面，一个长相清秀的男人坐在那里，身边有一只活狗，狗背上有一只活猫，

1236
00:57:50.460 --> 00:57:53.400
and the cat has an alive mouse on top of it.
而猫的背上还有一只活老鼠。

1237
00:57:54.180 --> 00:57:54.660
Yes.
是的。

1238
00:57:55.420 --> 00:57:59.740
Andy is going to spot this man and say, are you an actor?
安迪会发现这个男人并问，你是演员吗？

1239
00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:03.120
And he says, I'm not an actor, but I have an act.
他说，我不是演员，但我有表演节目。

1240
00:58:03.260 --> 00:58:04.940
It's dog-cat-mouse.
就是狗、猫、老鼠。

1241
00:58:05.880 --> 00:58:08.820
Andy says, is it hard to train them to do that?
安迪问，训练它们做这个很难吗？

1242
00:58:09.480 --> 00:58:12.940
And the man says, well, I've gone through a lot of mice.
那个男人说，嗯，我可是牺牲了很多只老鼠才练成的。

1243
00:58:13.500 --> 00:58:15.980
We got a fan question from Abilene R.
我们收到了来自田纳西州查塔努加市的艾比琳·R发来的粉丝提问，

1244
00:58:16.040 --> 00:58:17.880
in Chattanooga, Tennessee, who said,
她说，

1245
00:58:17.880 --> 00:58:22.200
oh, my God, is that Paul Feig at the casting office with the dog, cat, and mouse?
天哪，在选角办公室里带着狗、猫和老鼠的那个人是保罗·费格吗？

1246
00:58:22.340 --> 00:58:23.440
He's so funny.
他太搞笑了。

1247
00:58:23.760 --> 00:58:26.040
His talking head delivery was amazing.
他对着镜头独白的表现太棒了。

1248
00:58:26.220 --> 00:58:27.340
How did this come about?
这是怎么促成的？

1249
00:58:28.140 --> 00:58:31.680
Yes, Abilene, this was Paul Feig.
是的，艾比琳，那就是保罗·费格。

1250
00:58:32.120 --> 00:58:34.840
Greg wanted Paul to play this role.
格雷格想让保罗来演这个角色。

1251
00:58:35.620 --> 00:58:38.080
And he is so, so funny.
而且他真的、真的太搞笑了。

1252
00:58:38.260 --> 00:58:39.520
He's so funny.
他太搞笑了。

1253
00:58:39.720 --> 00:58:44.220
I thought we could hear his talking head, and then I would share the candy bag alts.
我想我们可以先听听他的访谈片段，然后我再分享糖果袋的备选方案。

1254
00:58:44.340 --> 00:58:45.140
I love it.
我喜欢这个。

1255
00:58:45.420 --> 00:58:47.680
Is it hard to train them to do that?
训练它们做那个很难吗？

1256
00:58:48.500 --> 00:58:49.760
You go through a lot of mice.
你们得用掉很多只老鼠吧。

1257
00:58:50.060 --> 00:58:52.840
It started by accident, actually, as these things tend to do.
其实这纯属偶然，这种事往往都是这样发生的。

1258
00:58:52.980 --> 00:58:55.680
I was sending out my cat, and I accidentally put her on top of my dog,
当时我正要把猫放出去，结果不小心把它放到了狗的背上，

1259
00:58:55.840 --> 00:58:57.680
and I was so mad at myself at firSt.
起初我对自己生气极了。

1260
00:58:57.800 --> 00:59:00.560
And I was like, wait, wait a second.
然后我心想，等等，等一下。

1261
00:59:04.640 --> 00:59:08.640
So that talking head was actually the candy bag alt.
所以那个访谈片段其实是糖果袋的备选方案。

1262
00:59:09.040 --> 00:59:09.480
Yes.
是的。

1263
00:59:09.920 --> 00:59:11.800
And he would have gone on to say,
他本来还会接着说，

1264
00:59:12.120 --> 00:59:14.800
my ex-wife tells everyone the mouse was her idea,
我前妻到处跟人说老鼠的主意是她出的，

1265
00:59:14.800 --> 00:59:16.960
but I don't have any recollection of that.
但我完全没印象。

1266
00:59:17.420 --> 00:59:19.220
Anyway, I would have thought of it myself.
总之，我自己也能想到。

1267
00:59:19.860 --> 00:59:22.160
And here were the other talking head options.
以下是其他访谈片段的备选方案。

1268
00:59:22.960 --> 00:59:25.200
I've done birthdays, retirement parties.
我做过生日派对、退休派对。

1269
00:59:25.220 --> 00:59:27.060
I did a shoe store opening once.
有一次我还给一家鞋店开业表演过。

1270
00:59:27.220 --> 00:59:32.040
I still try to live off just the money I get from performing in parking lots behind Cvs.
我至今仍尽量只靠在CVS药店后面的停车场表演赚来的钱生活。

1271
00:59:32.040 --> 00:59:36.880
And then everything beyond that is bonus, because you don't know when this could all go away.
除此之外的一切都是额外收入，因为你不知道这一切什么时候会结束。

1272
00:59:37.980 --> 00:59:39.040
Here's another one.
这是另一个。

1273
00:59:39.460 --> 00:59:45.820
I guess my realistic dream is to do a horse, dog, cat, mouse, all four in a column, you know?
我想我现实点的梦想是做成马、狗、猫、老鼠，四层叠罗汉，你懂吗？

1274
00:59:46.560 --> 00:59:55.160
And then sometimes, and I know how this sounds, but I imagine doing all four of those with like a piece of cheese on top of the mouse's hat.
有时候——我知道这听起来很荒谬——但我幻想着把这四个叠在一起，还在老鼠的帽子上放一块奶酪。

1275
00:59:55.480 --> 00:59:59.680
You wouldn't think the cheese is the hardest part, but all of them love cheese.
你可能想不到奶酪才是最难的部分，因为它们全都爱吃奶酪。

1276
01:00:00.360 --> 01:00:04.480
Well, Andy does ask, does anything go on top of the mouse?
嗯，安迪确实问了，老鼠头上会放东西吗？

1277
01:00:04.980 --> 01:00:07.040
And he says, yes, a little hat.
他说，会，一顶小帽子。

1278
01:00:07.680 --> 01:00:10.300
And then Andy asks if the mouse has a name.
然后安迪问老鼠有没有名字。

1279
01:00:10.640 --> 01:00:13.940
And the man says, it doesn't make sense to name the mice.
那个人说，给老鼠起名字没意义。

1280
01:00:14.480 --> 01:00:15.120
That's right.
没错。

1281
01:00:15.320 --> 01:00:18.940
And then Paul Feig improvised this line.
然后保罗·费格即兴发挥了这句台词。

1282
01:00:19.160 --> 01:00:21.220
They're kind of like cannon fodder, you know?
它们就像炮灰一样，你懂吗？

1283
01:00:21.520 --> 01:00:23.340
You're not one of those PETA guys, are you?
你不是那种善待动物组织的人吧？

1284
01:00:23.780 --> 01:00:26.840
And then the cat jumps off the dog, and he's like, ah, great.
然后猫从狗身上跳下来，他说，啊，太棒了。

1285
01:00:26.840 --> 01:00:34.420
We got a fan question from Karen T in North Carolina who said, I need to know everything about the mouse, the cat, and the dog.
我们收到了北卡罗来纳州凯伦·T发来的粉丝提问，她说，我需要知道关于那只老鼠、猫和狗的一切。

1286
01:00:34.580 --> 01:00:34.960
How?
怎么做到的？

1287
01:00:35.560 --> 01:00:42.700
And Lily B from Canada said, did the animals come from Bob Dunn's animal rentals, and did they already know how to do that,
来自加拿大的莉莉·B问，这些动物是来自鲍勃·邓恩动物租赁公司吗？它们本来就会做那个动作吗？

1288
01:00:42.720 --> 01:00:46.040
or were they specifically trained to do it for this episode?
还是为了这一集专门训练的？

1289
01:00:47.400 --> 01:00:51.480
Well, everyone, I'll have you know, I went deep on this.
好吧，各位，我得让你们知道，我在这方面深挖过了。

1290
01:00:51.740 --> 01:00:54.580
I found out everything about how they stacked these animals.
我查清了关于它们如何堆叠这些动物的一切。

1291
01:00:54.580 --> 01:00:58.000
I personally love animal stacking.
我个人非常喜欢动物堆叠。

1292
01:00:58.320 --> 01:01:08.140
Yeah, I feel like you should share about this, like how I love when animals are dressed as other animals, like if you dress your dog to look like a bunny, like for Halloween,
是啊，我觉得你应该分享一下这个，就像我喜欢动物打扮成其他动物一样，比如万圣节时把你家狗打扮成兔子的样子，

1293
01:01:08.300 --> 01:01:09.000
I love that.
我喜欢那个。

1294
01:01:09.240 --> 01:01:13.120
I love pictures of animals stacked on other animals, paintings.
我喜欢动物叠在其他动物身上的照片和画作。

1295
01:01:13.580 --> 01:01:18.180
And oddly, I have a painting of animals stacked on each other.
奇怪的是，我刚好有一幅动物叠在一起的画。

1296
01:01:18.320 --> 01:01:18.700
I know.
我知道。

1297
01:01:19.060 --> 01:01:22.720
My friend Alex and I, we both love animal stacking.
我和我的朋友亚历克斯，我们都喜欢动物堆叠。

1298
01:01:22.720 --> 01:01:25.500
We send each other pictures of different stacks of animals.
我们经常互发各种动物堆叠的照片。

1299
01:01:25.860 --> 01:01:26.580
You know what?
你知道吗？

1300
01:01:26.700 --> 01:01:33.580
I love any video of like a cat on top of a goat or like a dog on top of a cow.
我喜欢任何猫骑在羊身上，或者狗骑在牛身上的视频。

1301
01:01:33.580 --> 01:01:34.620
I don't know.
我不知道。

1302
01:01:34.800 --> 01:01:37.940
I just like it when they ride on one another.
我就是喜欢看它们叠在一起骑着的样子。

1303
01:01:37.940 --> 01:01:38.840
I don't know.
我不知道。

1304
01:01:39.080 --> 01:01:41.980
What's your favorite animal stacking that you've seen?
你见过最喜欢的动物叠罗汉是什么样的？

1305
01:01:41.980 --> 01:01:44.200
Oh, that's a good question.
噢，这是个好问题。

1306
01:01:44.600 --> 01:01:54.180
There was this video I saw of this cat that used to love to go out into this herd of sheep and just ride around on their backs.
我曾看过一个视频，有只猫特别喜欢跑到羊群里，骑在它们的背上到处转悠。

1307
01:01:54.480 --> 01:01:55.780
Oh, that's cute.
噢，那太可爱了。

1308
01:01:56.080 --> 01:01:57.700
It just and it loved them.
它就是……而且它很喜欢它们。

1309
01:01:57.900 --> 01:02:00.940
But sometimes it would just take a nap on top of a sheep.
但有时候它会直接趴在羊背上打个盹。

1310
01:02:01.200 --> 01:02:01.580
Come on.
得了吧。

1311
01:02:01.580 --> 01:02:02.400
And clean itself.
还会给自己梳理毛发。

1312
01:02:02.800 --> 01:02:05.540
I love it when animals are friends with each other.
我喜欢看动物之间成为朋友。

1313
01:02:05.840 --> 01:02:06.140
Right.
没错。

1314
01:02:06.280 --> 01:02:09.140
We should say you like it when animals choose to be stacked.
我们应该说你喜欢看动物主动叠在一起。

1315
01:02:09.480 --> 01:02:10.300
Oh, yes.
噢，是的。

1316
01:02:10.440 --> 01:02:10.760
Right?
对吧？

1317
01:02:11.800 --> 01:02:13.600
Not for stacking.
不是为了叠罗汉。

1318
01:02:13.820 --> 01:02:15.620
I don't love for stacking, no.
我不喜欢叠罗汉，不。

1319
01:02:16.400 --> 01:02:20.880
As for the fan questions, yes, the dog cat mouse came from Bob Dunn's animals.
至于粉丝提问，是的，那只狗、猫和老鼠来自鲍勃·邓恩的动物训练中心。

1320
01:02:21.040 --> 01:02:24.080
And yes, they were specifically trained for this episode.
而且没错，它们是专门为这一集训练的。

1321
01:02:24.520 --> 01:02:25.940
Here's how it happened.
事情是这样的。

1322
01:02:26.500 --> 01:02:35.800
When Steve Burgess got this script, he reached out to Bob Dunn's and he sent them a video of a real dog cat mouse that the writers had seen.
当史蒂夫·伯吉斯拿到剧本后，他联系了鲍勃·邓恩，并给他们发了一个编剧们看过的真实狗猫鼠视频。

1323
01:02:35.800 --> 01:02:37.460
I googled it.
我谷歌了一下。

1324
01:02:37.980 --> 01:02:41.780
There is a very famous dog cat mouse man from Bisbee, Arizona.
亚利桑那州比斯比有个非常有名的狗猫鼠艺人。

1325
01:02:42.340 --> 01:02:42.800
Oh.
噢。

1326
01:02:42.800 --> 01:02:52.800
His name is Greg Pike, and he will set up on a sidewalk with his dog cat mouse, and he'll accept donations from anyone who wants to take a picture with them.
他叫格雷格·派克，他会带着他的狗、猫和老鼠在人行道上摆好阵势，接受任何想跟它们合影的人的捐款。

1327
01:02:53.020 --> 01:02:54.980
His dog's name is Booger.
他的狗叫布格。

1328
01:02:55.220 --> 01:02:56.900
His cat's name is Kitty.
他的猫叫基蒂。

1329
01:02:57.120 --> 01:02:58.960
And his mouse's name is Mousy.
他的老鼠叫毛西。

1330
01:02:59.060 --> 01:03:00.300
And they all stand together.
它们就那样站在一起。

1331
01:03:00.300 --> 01:03:03.000
So this might have been the inspiration.
所以这可能就是灵感来源。

1332
01:03:03.260 --> 01:03:03.660
Got it.
明白了。

1333
01:03:03.660 --> 01:03:04.880
And the town loves him.
而且镇上的人都很喜欢他。

1334
01:03:05.160 --> 01:03:07.360
The town loves Greg and his animal stack.
镇上的人都很喜欢格雷格和他的动物叠罗汉。

1335
01:03:07.920 --> 01:03:13.420
Steve said that Bob Dunn's initially offered a stack of dog cat rat.
史蒂夫说，鲍勃·邓恩最初提供的是狗、猫和老鼠的组合。

1336
01:03:14.120 --> 01:03:16.940
Rats are very smart, and they're very easy to train.
老鼠非常聪明，而且很容易训练。

1337
01:03:17.280 --> 01:03:24.360
They sent over a picture of what a dog cat rat might look like, and the writers really wanted a mouse.
他们发来了一张狗、猫和老鼠叠在一起的照片，但编剧们真的很想要一只老鼠。

1338
01:03:25.240 --> 01:03:25.720
Yeah.
是啊。

1339
01:03:26.160 --> 01:03:27.160
I don't know.
我不知道。

1340
01:03:27.340 --> 01:03:29.220
Like, a mouse is so tiny.
就是，老鼠太小了。

1341
01:03:29.460 --> 01:03:30.240
It kind of like—
它有点像……

1342
01:03:30.240 --> 01:03:32.160
And then the little top hat's even tinier.
而且那顶小礼帽更小。

1343
01:03:32.260 --> 01:03:33.240
It's even so smaller.
甚至还要更小。

1344
01:03:33.460 --> 01:03:33.580
Yeah.
是啊。

1345
01:03:34.200 --> 01:03:39.620
Well, Steve wrote to them and said, hey, we would really like to try for a mouse on top of the cat.
好吧，史蒂夫写信给他们说，嘿，我们真的很想尝试让老鼠待在猫的上面。

1346
01:03:40.020 --> 01:03:43.740
The rat could be a backup, but our first choice is mouse.
老鼠可以作为备选，但我们的首选是老鼠。

1347
01:03:44.080 --> 01:03:45.880
These are the emails Steve Burgess writes.
这就是史蒂夫·伯吉斯写的邮件。

1348
01:03:46.160 --> 01:03:46.300
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1349
01:03:46.680 --> 01:03:50.060
Bob Dunn wrote back, Steve, mouse's first choice.
鲍勃·邓恩回信说，史蒂夫，老鼠是首选。

1350
01:03:50.260 --> 01:03:51.220
We'll let the mouse know.
我们会通知那只老鼠的。

1351
01:03:52.060 --> 01:03:53.240
That's what he wrote back.
这就是他回信的内容。

1352
01:03:54.400 --> 01:04:00.460
Well, Ange, I have even more information to share because remember when I did that AT&T commercial
安吉，我还有更多信息要分享，还记得我拍那个AT&T广告的时候吗

1353
01:04:00.460 --> 01:04:03.400
and there was that pug from Bob Dunn's?
当时鲍勃·邓恩动物训练中心有一只哈巴狗？

1354
01:04:03.640 --> 01:04:07.240
I told them, I am going to reach out to you for this podcaSt.
我告诉他们，我会为了这档播客联系你们。

1355
01:04:07.720 --> 01:04:08.880
Well, I reached out.
结果，我真的联系了。

1356
01:04:09.380 --> 01:04:11.840
I said, how did you stack these animals?
我问他们，你们是怎么把这些动物叠在一起的？

1357
01:04:12.780 --> 01:04:18.400
Well, Mike Morris, the head animal trainer at Bob Dunn's, wrote me back and said this.
鲍勃·邓恩动物训练中心的首席动物训练师迈克·莫里斯回信告诉了我这些。

1358
01:04:18.980 --> 01:04:19.500
Hello.
你好。

1359
01:04:19.500 --> 01:04:24.260
Oh, even though I didn't do this job myself, I remember it vividly because it was such a
虽然那次工作不是我亲自做的，但我记忆犹新，因为那场景太搞笑了，

1360
01:04:24.260 --> 01:04:28.360
